Wow.  So you have chosen a really very difficult conduct.  And one of 
the kind I don't like...  For you are bound to rely on luck to some 
extent.  A series of three arch liches in Gehennom can easily take all 
your armour away...

> For the feared Touch of Death, I intend to use "oLS and any means of
> hallucination (potions, blessed tins of violet fungus, whatever).

You may need quite a number of "oLS, then.  Concerning hallucination, I 
don't really see it as a sensible means.  For who is using the touch of 
death on you most of the time?  The wizard.  If you hallucinate, you 
will not be able to distinguish him from his pets, so it will be very 
difficult to kill him.  Also, when will you drink your potion?  If you 
drink it before you fight him, you may just not be able to kill him, 
since you don't know whom to kill.  And if it wears off while he is 
still alive, he may kill you instantly.  It seems to me that then you 
should always try to kill him in one hit, using a /oD.  But if you miss 
him with the first zap, which will happen from time to time, he gets a 
chance to instakill you in the next move.

If you wear an "oLS, you cannot wear an "oR.  Which means you have to 
rely on silver dragon scale mail for reflection.  "The arch lich touches 
you!  Your silver dragon scale mail disintegrates... "  Next you may be 
hit by a bolt of lightning destroying your wands of death or whatever. 
I guess you need to place some spare dragon armor in stashes all around 
the dungeon...  And have many wands of death.

